],[530.0,0.8043],[535.0,0.8713],[540.0,0.905],[545.0,0.8657],[550.0,0.7909],[555.0,0.749],[560.0,0.7108],[565.0,0.6167],[570.0,0.4321],[575.0,0.1614],[580.0,-0.2152],[585.0,-0.6832],[590.0,-0.721]],"r":[[560.0,-0.7376],[565.0,-0.6356],[570.0,-0.4666],[575.0,-0.2689],[580.0,-0.0606],[585.0,0.1478],[590.0,0.3365],[595.0,0.4775],[600.0,0.5549],[605.0,0.6111],[610.0,0.6487],[615.0,0.6715],[620.0,0.6787],[625.0,0.6727],[630.0,0.6501],[635.0,0.6058],[640.0,0.502],[645.0,0.3015],[650.0,0.017],[655.0,-0.3818],[660.0,-0.448]]},"source":{"document":"013Ai158A","date":"1996-03","file":"fuji-reala-ace.pdf","url":"https://asset.fujifilm.com/www/jp/files/2024-04/2dca996da7fa6b3e34edda4c943870c2/datasheet_realaace_01.pdf","sha256":"04bb3116657b2263aa19682ff56cb41c779ed14931272325d42e9f753b64b918"},"notes":["Fujifilm data sheet (Japanese), page 4 plots; reference number 013Ai158A, date read from the print code (\u55b6\u6280\u30fb96.3-HB). Film sold as Reala Ace (with a fourth, cyan-sensitive layer).","Characteristic curves: daylight exposure 1/125 s, process CN-16X, Status M equivalent. x axis is log H in lux-seconds as printed (axis runs -3.5 to 1.0); b/g/r are three black solid vector curves (blue on top, red lowest, labelled \u9752/\u7dd1/\u8d64), drawn from log H about -3.2 to 0.5 only.","Spectral sensitivity: the sheet has no numbers on the y axis, only a scale arrow marking 1.0 (log unit) between two horizontal rules; y is therefore relative log sensitivity with 0 set at the lower rule and 1.0 at the upper rule (absolute offset not printed). Sensitivity is the reciprocal of the exposure (ergs/cm2, as printed on this sheet) needed for a specified density (minimum density + 1.0). All curves are black; the dashed curve of the cyan-sensitive layer (\u30b7\u30a2\u30f3\u611f\u5149\u5c64) is traced as line l4 (build.py ignores it). Each layer curve ends in near-vertical drops (b ends about 378-396 nm, g about 480-586 nm, r about 560-657 nm, l4 about 480-561 nm), so the last few nm are approximated on the 5 nm grid; the b/g/l4 curves cross each other near 485-500 nm.","Spectral dye density plot has only 'mid' (\u4e2d\u9593\u6fc3\u5ea6, density given by a neutral subject) and 'min' (\u6700\u5c0f\u6fc3\u5ea6, minimum density), no separate c/m/y dyes; the curves run about 392-724 nm.","Grain: diffuse RMS granularity 4 (printed as '\u2026\u20264' next to heading 10); micro-densitometer aperture 48 um, sample density minimum density + 1.0. Film speed ISO 100/21 deg daylight (tungsten 3200 K: ISO 25 with LBB-12). No paper is named on the sheet except 'Fujicolor paper'."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":16.0,"grain_size":20.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}